{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the way at the inn.</b> The word ויהי refers back to Moses, and Scripture tells you that when Moses was on the way at the inn, ויפגשהו ה׳ — 'and HaShem met him' — this is an angel, and he is called by the special Name, and he is from the 'separate beings' (ha-nifradim), not from the 'plantings' (ha-neti'ot); yet despite this he is called by the special Name, since he was sent to complete and to do the will of his Maker, blessed be He. And so they said in the Midrash: ויהי בדרך במלון — beloved is circumcision, for Moses was not given even a single hour's respite on its account, because he was on the road and delayed circumcising Eliezer his son; immediately <b>HaShem met him and sought to kill him</b> — Moses. You find that it was an angel of mercy, and despite this, ויבקש המיתו. Said Rabbi Yosi: heaven forfend, Moses did not delay; rather he said: if I circumcise and then set out on the road, it is dangerous for the infant for three days; if I circumcise and delay three days, the Holy One, blessed be He, has commanded me, 'Go back to Egypt' — so why was he punished? Because he occupied himself with the inn first, that is, he should have circumcised him first and afterward arranged his lodging, for one does not pass over a commandment. And the meaning of 'angel of mercy' is that he was an emissary of the attribute of mercy." "<b>And know</b> that according to this Midrash there is reason to wonder: since Moses was at the inn, why does it say ותקח צפורה צור — 'and Tziporah took a flint' — when it would be fitting for Moses himself to engage in the commandment? Therefore our Rabbi Chananel, of blessed memory, explained that Moses was not there at the inn, for as it said above: ויקח משה את אשתו ואת בניו וירכיבם על החמור — 'and Moses took his wife and his sons and set them on the donkey' — and the meaning of the verse is that he sent them ahead of him, and afterward וישב משה מצרימה — 'and Moses returned to Egypt'; and if so, Moses was not now at the inn. And it says ויבקש המיתו, that is, against the lad, for the angel made itself like a serpent and swallowed him from his head to his thighs, and again swallowed him from his feet to the place of circumcision, and then ותקח צפורה צור, for she understood that the punishment was because she had delayed the time of the commandment and had not circumcised him on the eighth day. Thus explained our Rabbi Chananel, of blessed memory, at the beginning of the parashah of וישמע יתרו. And in the commentary of Rashi, of blessed memory, I saw that Moses was at the inn, but he was ill and unable to circumcise him, and Tziporah circumcised him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:17.043140339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}